 "notes": "Microwave light-shining-through-wall (LSW) experiment. Main result = ALP-photon coupling exclusion from Fig.13 (ALP_excl_plot.pdf vector figure, CROWS 06/2013 blue region). Boundary traced from the blue fill path; x/y log calibration reproduces both quoted numbers: wideband g=9.9e-8 GeV^-1 (flat, mass-independent below resonance) and most-sensitive g=4.5e-8 GeV^-1 at the resonance mass m_a=hf_sys=7.2e-6 eV (f_sys=1.73999 GHz). x-axis anchored so the resonance dip lands at 7.196e-6 eV. Curve is flat ~9.8e-8 at low mass, dips to 4.5e-8 at resonance, then rises steeply above resonance due to exponential suppression of the form factor (k prime imaginary for m>hf_sys). Paper also sets a hidden-photon limit chi=4.1e-9 at 10.8 ueV (Fig.14, DarkPhoton) - not reported here as the abstract/Fig.13 present the ALP result first. Not a DM search: density-independent.",
